From 4c40255cad87cb58e1e9e37fb4e076263119fc93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:58:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec: use non-MPD PAS ID for
 IPQ5018

WCSS_PAS_ID will bring up both Q6 and WCSS subsystem.

In MultiPD arch, MPD_WCSS_PAS_ID only bring up Q6 subsystem  whlile the
WCSS subsystem belongs to UserPD1, becuase it only control the internal
2.4G WiFi. The driver will bring up it through a TZ call durning UserPD1
start sequence.

Signed-off-by: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
@@ -414,7 +414,7 @@ static const struct wcss_data wcss_sec_i
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id wcss_sec_of_match[] = {
-	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipq5018-wcss-sec-pil", .data = &wcss_sec_ipq5332_res_init },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipq5018-wcss-sec-pil", .data = &wcss_sec_ipq9574_res_init },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipq5332-wcss-sec-pil", .data = &wcss_sec_ipq5332_res_init },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipq5424-wcss-sec-pil", .data = &wcss_sec_ipq5424_res_init },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipq9574-wcss-sec-pil", .data = &wcss_sec_ipq9574_res_init },
